	(text "RJ45 CABLE MAPPER  rev A  rixnobis"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f78d4654-5d37-4e94-9d2f-ef08888d62be")
	)
	(text "Touch a flying wire to PAD1; the LED for its 8P8C pin lights. ULN2803A sinks each\nLED. PAD at 5V through 1k, so a wire grounded at the far end draws 5 mA, not a short.\nA finger bridging pad and wire (~1 Mohm) holds the ULN input under 0.1 V, far below the\ntwo-VBE turn-on, so only metal-to-metal contact lights an LED. Two shorted wires light two."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "733ccb30-625f-43c0-a9a7-da0be4962a06")
	)
	(text "The RJ45 jack is the only through-hole part: an unshielded right-angle 8P8C on the\nTE 5555164 / Amphenol 54602 land pattern, supplied and hand-soldered by the builder.\nEverything else is SMD, JLC-assembled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bf3ad9ff-1ae6-4607-9f54-49a08c538c4a")
	)
